-- title:
--   Cyclotomic determinant of the Hecke-side Galois representation
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$, a finite set $S$ of natural numbers, a complete discrete valuation ring $\mathcal{O}$ (a domain, discrete valuation ring, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology), a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, and a noetherian local ring $T$, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra with local structure map and is finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module. Assume $p$ is a prime with $(p : \mathcal{O})$ in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $H$ be a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) for these data, that is: a ring homomorphism $\pi : \mathbb{T} \to T$ reducing to $\theta$ after the residue-field map of $\mathcal{O} \to T$, with $\mathcal{O}[\operatorname{im}\pi] = T$, such that every $\theta$-lifting character $\mathbb{T} \to \mathcal{O}$ factors through an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $T \to \mathcal{O}$ composed with $\pi$, with $\mathcal{O} \to T$ inducing a surjection onto the residue field of $T$; together with a rank-two adically continuous representation $\rho$ of $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ on a finite free $T$-module whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible and which satisfies, for each prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, each valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit in $A$ and each $\sigma$ acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^\ell$, the identity $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma)) = X^2 - \pi(T_\ell) X + \ell$. The conclusion is `H.ρ.DetIsCyclotomic p`: the image of $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $T$, and for every $n$, every $\sigma \in \operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ and every natural number $a$ such that $\sigma\mu = \mu^a$ for all $p^n$-th roots of unity $\mu$, one has $\det \rho(\sigma) - a \in (p^n)T$.
--
--   This identifies the determinant of the Galois representation carried by a Hecke-algebra datum with the $p$-adic cyclotomic character, in the congruence form used by the deformation-theoretic local conditions. It is the input that lets the Hecke-side representation be compared with deformations of prescribed determinant, and is invoked in the ordinary and flat local-condition arguments and in the identification of local Hecke rings.
